  "verbalization": "Mefenamic Acid appears to interact with Akr1c3 through a series of mechanistic pathways involving the enzyme Akr1c2 or Akr1c1. The drug binds to Akr1c2 or Akr1c1, which in turn participates in the phenanthrene 9,10-monooxygenase activity, a process that is also engaged by Akr1c3. This suggests a potential functional link between Mefenamic Acid and Akr1c3, where the drug may influence the activity of the enzyme complex involving Akr1c1 or Akr1c2. The shared involvement of Akr1c3 in the same metabolic pathway implies that the drug could modulate the activity of this enzyme complex, potentially affecting the metabolism of phenanthrene derivatives or other substrates. The evidence is consistent with a direct interaction between Mefenamic Acid and Akr1c3, supported by the observed binding and participation in the same metabolic pathway. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple overlapping pathways, which strengthens the hypothesis that Mefenamic Acid may exert its effects through a shared functional role with Akr1c3.",
